---
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="How Inferno Tips handles account details, drill results, public scores and browser storage, and how to request deletion."
    />
    <title>Privacy Policy — Inferno Tips</title>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="credits-page">
      <a href="/">← Back to Inferno Tips</a>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>
        Last updated: <time datetime="2026-09-21">21 September 2026</time>
      </p>
      <p>
        Inferno Tips is operated by Oliver Atkinson, who is responsible for the
        personal information described here. For privacy questions, correction
        or deletion requests, email{' '}
        <a href="mailto:tos@inferno.tips">tos@inferno.tips</a>. Signing in is
        optional. You can practise with progress saved only in your browser.
      </p>
      <h2>Discord sign-in and account data</h2>
      <p>
        Where account sign-in is available, we receive your Discord user ID,
        name, email address, email verification status and profile image URL. We
        store these details with account timestamps, encrypted provider tokens
        and sign-in sessions. Session records can include your IP address and
        browser’s user-agent information to manage and protect access. We do not
        request your password, Discord messages, friends or server list.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use this information to identify your account and save progress
        across devices. Your account email, Discord identifier and profile
        details are not published on leaderboards. Discord processes your
        sign-in under its{' '}
        <a href="https://discord.com/privacy">own privacy policy</a>. We do not
        send your drill history to Discord.
      </p>
      <h2>Drill results and public scores</h2>
      <p>
        Signed-in drills send prayer, movement and supply inputs to our server
        for validation. We retain lesson identifiers, results, timing, feedback
        and validation records. If you choose to import browser history, we
        store it separately as unverified history. It cannot grant verified
        passes or leaderboard scores.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ranked runs send gameplay inputs and timing for score validation, even
        when you are not signed in. If you choose to publish a result, your
        chosen display name, score, mode, stage and ranking information become
        public. A guest identifier links scores to your browser; signing in can
        associate those scores with your account. Avoid putting personal details
        in your public name.
      </p>
      <p>
        Signed-in scores use your saved public nickname. We generate a random
        three-word nickname to start with; it is separate from your Discord
        profile name and email. You can change it in Account settings, which
        also updates the name shown on your existing account leaderboard
        entries. Nicknames are not unique and do not determine account
        ownership.
      </p>
      <h2>Browser storage and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Your keybinds, sound settings and browser-only progress are stored on
        your device. Pending uploads are kept there for retry. Clearing browser
        data can remove these settings and unsynced results.
      </p>
      <p>
        Essential cookies maintain sign-in sessions and ownership of guest
        scores. Account sessions expire after 14 days unless renewed through
        use; the guest-score cookie can last a year. Short-lived cookies also
        protect the sign-in process. Blocking these cookies prevents the
        associated account or score-saving features from working.
      </p>
      <h2>Hosting and abuse prevention</h2>
      <p>
        Cloudflare hosts the website, API and database. It processes network and
        request information, including IP addresses, browser information and
        diagnostic logs, to deliver and protect the service. Turnstile performs
        abuse checks when signing in, publishing scores or deleting an account.
        We also limit requests by IP address and account. See{' '}
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">
          Cloudflare’s privacy policy
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <p>
        We use personal data to provide the account and score features you
        request, and in our legitimate interests to maintain a secure, reliable
        service and prevent score manipulation. We do not sell your personal
        data or use your Discord information for advertising. Access is limited
        to operating and supporting the service, our service providers, and
        disclosures required by law.
      </p>
      <p>
        Cloudflare and Discord operate internationally and may process data
        outside your country, including the United States. Cloudflare describes
        its processing and international-transfer safeguards in its{' '}
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-customer-dpa/">
          Data Processing Addendum
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Account details, completed drill summaries and imported history remain
          while you keep your account, unless you request deletion.
        </li>
        <li>
          Unfinished account drills and unpublished ranked-run records are
          removed by scheduled cleanup after 30 days. Ranked-run input batches
          are also cleared after 30 days.
        </li>
        <li>
          Published scores and their supporting run records remain for
          leaderboard history until deleted. Removing a score from public view
          hides it; it does not by itself erase the stored record.
        </li>
        <li>
          Expired account sessions and sign-in verification records are cleared
          by scheduled cleanup. Browser data remains until you clear it or the
          app removes expired pending uploads.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Provider backups and operational logs may retain copies temporarily
        under the provider’s retention arrangements after deletion from the live
        database. Security records may be retained where needed to investigate
        abuse or meet legal obligations.
      </p>
      <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        Where accounts are enabled, Account settings let you sign out on all
        devices, export account details and up to 10,000 recent drill summaries,
        or delete your account and linked public scores. The export is a
        convenience tool; you can contact us for a fuller access request.
        Deleting your account does not clear data stored in your browser or
        delete your Discord account.
      </p>
      <p>
        The High scores page lets you remove your scores from public view using
        the browser or account that owns them. For deletion of guest-score
        records, or if you cannot access your account, email{' '}
        <a href="mailto:tos@inferno.tips">tos@inferno.tips</a>. We may need to
        confirm ownership before acting. Do not send passwords or sign-in
        tokens.
      </p>
      <p>
        Depending on applicable law, you can request access, correction,
        deletion or a portable copy of your data, and object to or request
        restrictions on certain processing. Contact us to exercise these rights.
        You can also complain to your local data protection authority, including
        the UK’s{' '}
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">
          Information Commissioner’s Office
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <h2>Staging and updates</h2>
      <p>
        This policy also applies to our staging site. Staging accounts and
        scores are stored separately from production. Changes to this policy
        will appear here with an updated date; material changes will also be
        called out on the site.
      </p>
      <nav aria-label="Policy pages">
        <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a> ·{' '}
        <a href="/credits/">Credits & sources</a>
      </nav>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
